  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizationsorganizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Independent, representative, effective and sustainable employer and business membership organizations have a critical role to play in labour market governance. This biennium the ILO has continued to support the Kiribati Chamber of Commerce and Industry (KCCI) to strengthen its institutional and organizational capacities. Notable initiatives include technical assistance and support for a feasiblity assessment of the proposal for a &quot;buy local&quot; initiative to stimulate domestic private sector development; support for the development and deployment of customized membership management software; and scholarships for KCCI representatives to participate in ITC-ILO training courses, including the Masters Training in Management of EBMO.</narrative>
  </description>
